<h1>Knome Enterprise Knowledge Platform</h1>
<p style="font-size: 14pt; color: #475569; margin-top: -6px;"><strong>Architecture Specification, Role-Permissions Matrix & Content Workflows</strong></p>

<div class="meta-box">
  <strong>Enterprise Organization:</strong> MPOnline Limited (Govt. of Madhya Pradesh Partner)<br>
  <strong>System Name:</strong> Knome Collaborative Intranet & Enterprise Knowledge Hub<br>
  <strong>Classification:</strong> Internal Enterprise Architecture Standard & Governance Guide<br>
  <strong>Document Version:</strong> 3.0 (October 2026)<br>
  <strong>Authorized By:</strong> Platform Architecture & IT Security Committee
</div>

<hr>

<h2>1. Platform Architectural Mapping ("Knome Which Which Thing")</h2>
<p>Knome consolidates the capabilities of major modern digital platforms into an integrated, compliant internal enterprise environment for MPOnline:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Platform Inspiration</th>
      <th style="width: 25%;">Knome Feature Module</th>
      <th style="width: 50%;">Detailed Enterprise Capabilities</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>1. LinkedIn</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Feed Posts & Clips</strong></td>
      <td>
        • <strong>Feed Posts:</strong> Instant status updates (rich text / up to 400 chars), media attachments (images up to 25MB, documents up to 400MB), @mentions, #hashtags, and targeted audience scoping (Public, Connections, or Specific Community).<br>
        • <strong>Clips:</strong> Full-screen vertical short-form reels with creator profile links, instant reactions, comments, and views counter.<br>
        • <strong>Professional Identity:</strong> Colleague directory, Follow / Connect networking requests, skill tags, and DPDP Act 2023 privacy controls.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2. Stack Overflow</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Articles & Karma Engine</strong></td>
      <td>
        • <strong>Long-Form Technical Articles:</strong> Rich Markdown editor with live preview, syntax-highlighted code blocks, cover banner uploads, reading time estimates, and departmental taxonomy.<br>
        • <strong>Karma Gamification & Reputation Engine:</strong> Point rewards (+10 Post, +25 Article, +2 Like, daily streaks), Badge tiers (Bronze, Silver, Gold, Platinum), and monthly departmental leaderboards.<br>
        • <strong>Q&A & Discussions:</strong> Nested threaded comments, technical problem solving, and solution upvotes.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>3. Knome (TCS Enterprise)</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Enterprise Wiki & SOPs</strong></td>
      <td>
        • <strong>Enterprise Wiki Repository:</strong> Centralized departmental documentation, standard operating procedures (SOPs), project technical specifications, and knowledge continuity.<br>
        • <strong>Pre-Publication Clearance:</strong> Formal peer and moderator approval workflow ensuring high standards of technical governance before publication.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>4. YouTube</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Videos & Podcasts</strong></td>
      <td>
        • <strong>Video Knowledge Hub:</strong> Multimedia video streaming library (MP4, MOV, WebM up to 500MB), watch modals, and engagement metrics.<br>
        • <strong>Podcasts & Global Audio Player:</strong> Audio series and episode tracks. Equipped with a persistent <strong>Global Audio Player</strong> running at the bottom of the viewport so audio plays without interruption as users browse through other pages.
      </td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>5. Employee Hub</strong></td>
      <td><strong>Internal Careers & Openings</strong></td>
      <td>
        • <strong>Internal Job Openings:</strong> Vacancies published by HR across MPOnline departments, candidate eligibility criteria, application deadlines, self-service applications, and automated deadline archiving.<br>
        • <strong>Broadcast Alerts:</strong> Organization-wide critical corporate banners with real-time SignalR push notifications for town halls, emergency notices, or policy changes.<br>
        • <strong>Communities:</strong> Public and Private departmental interest channels with membership approval clearance.
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<hr>

<h2>2. Complete Roles & Permissions Matrix ("Yeh Kya Kya Kar Sakte Hai")</h2>

<h3>2.1 The 5 Platform Roles</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Employee (<code>EMP</code>):</strong> Standard self-service workplace account for all employees.</li>
  <li><strong>Community Admin (<code>CADM</code>):</strong> Channel leader managing membership, pinned content, and community-level guidelines.</li>
  <li><strong>Moderator (<code>MOD</code>):</strong> Content safety steward reviewing flagged items, approving articles/wiki/podcasts, and escalating suspensions.</li>
  <li><strong>HR Administrator (<code>HRADM</code>):</strong> Workforce operations leader managing job openings, broadcast announcements, community proposals, and direct employee account suspensions with custom durations.</li>
  <li><strong>System Administrator (<code>SYSADM</code>):</strong> Master security administrator overseeing role assignments, audit logs, keyword security, and infrastructure health.</li>
</ul>

