<h2>3. End-to-End Content & Disciplinary Workflows</h2>

<h3>3.1 Workflow 1: Direct Publishing (Feed Posts & Clips)</h3>
<div class="workflow-box">
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 1:</span> Employee creates Post or uploads a vertical Clip.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 2:</span> Client-side scanner verifies text for forbidden keywords or raw PII leaks (Aadhaar, PAN, AWS credentials).</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 3:</span> <strong>Direct Instant Publishing:</strong> Post/Clip goes live immediately on the public feed or targeted community channel with zero administrative delay.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 4:</span> Employee is rewarded with <strong>+10 Karma points</strong>; real-time notifications are pushed via SignalR.</p>
</div>

<h3>3.2 Workflow 2: Moderated Content Approval (Articles, Wiki, Videos & Podcasts)</h3>
<div class="workflow-box">
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 1:</span> Employee drafts an Article, Wiki entry, Video, or Podcast episode.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 2:</span> Employee clicks "Submit for Review". Content status is marked as <code>Pending Approval</code>.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 3:</span> Content queues in the Moderator's <strong>Media & Article Approvals Queue</strong> in the Moderation Console.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 4:</span> Moderator inspects the content for technical accuracy, formatting, and community compliance.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 5 (Resolution):</span></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Approved:</strong> Content goes live in the public catalog immediately. Author earns <strong>+25 Karma points</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Declined:</strong> Content is returned to the author's private drafts with actionable feedback notes.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h3>3.3 Workflow 3: Report Abuse & HR Admin Suspension Governance</h3>
<div class="governance-box">
  <p><strong>Platform Governance Principle:</strong> Strict separation of powers between Moderator investigation and HR Administrator disciplinary execution.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 1 (Flagging):</span> Any employee notices violating or toxic content and clicks <strong>Report Post / Clip / Comment</strong>, specifying violation reason and explanation.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 2 (Investigation):</span> The report appears in the <strong>Content Moderation Queue</strong>. The Moderator reviews the post snapshot, AI severity score, and author details.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 3 (Moderator Action):</span></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Dismiss:</strong> If the content is compliant, mark report as resolved.</li>
    <li><strong>Remove Content:</strong> Moderator immediately deletes the violating post/clip to prevent further dissemination.</li>
    <li><strong>Escalate Suspension:</strong> If disciplinary action is needed, Moderator clicks <strong>"Request Suspension"</strong>. This submits a formal governance request with evidence directly to HR Administrators.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 4 (HR Admin Review):</span> HR Admin navigates to <code>Admin Console ➔ Suspension Requests</code>.</p>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 5 (HR Admin Decision):</span></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Reject Request:</strong> HR Admin provides a mandatory audit note. Request is marked Rejected; employee remains active.</li>
    <li><strong>Confirm Suspension:</strong> HR Admin opens the <strong>Suspend Employee Account</strong> modal. <strong>Only HR Administrators</strong> have access to configure the suspension duration:
      <ul>
        <li><code>1 Day</code> (24 Hours cooldown)</li>
        <li><code>3 Days</code> (Short break)</li>
        <li><code>7 Days</code> (1 Week - Standard governance)</li>
        <li><code>14 Days</code> (2 Weeks)</li>
        <li><code>30 Days</code> (1 Month)</li>
        <li><code>Indefinite</code> (Until manual executive review)</li>
        <li><code>Custom End Date</code> (Exact calendar reinstatement date)</li>
      </ul>
      HR Admin enters a justification note and clicks <strong>Confirm Suspension</strong>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p><span class="flow-step">Step 6 (Instant Lockout):</span> The employee's JWT token is instantly revoked by backend <code>SuspensionGuard</code> middleware, terminating active sessions immediately across all devices.</p>
</div>

<hr>

<h2>4. Technical Infrastructure Overview</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> React 19, Tailwind CSS, Lucide Icons, Google Material Symbols, Vite</li>
  <li><strong>Backend:</strong> ASP.NET Core (.NET 10), Entity Framework Core, Clean Architecture</li>
  <li><strong>Database:</strong> Microsoft SQL Server (MSSQL) with full relational integrity and audit triggers</li>
  <li><strong>Real-Time Delivery:</strong> SignalR WebSocket hub for immediate notification delivery and broadcast alerts</li>
  <li><strong>Security Compliance:</strong> JWT Bearer Authentication, Whistleblower Protections, DPDP Act 2023</li>
</ul>

